// prelude unit limits (DESIGN.md sec:verification, "Budgets"; written by step
// M0.11): the minimum resource limits of compile-time evaluation, as the C
// standard sets translation limits. A conforming compiler never rejects an
// evaluation within all three; past them, running out is a build failure,
// reported as the machine's and not as a rejection of the program. The
// Rust-hosted copy is zed_kernel::eval::MIN_* in crates/zed-kernel/src/eval.rs.

// Steps of the definitional interpreter, whose strategy is fixed: one step per
// function call, `fix` round and `gen` step.
minSteps = 10000000;

// Bytes of memory: 1 GiB.
minMemory = 1073741824;

// Calls nested in one another.
minNestedCalls = 20000;
